Paper Stack

(CV, NLP, LLM, VLM, Diffusion, Agentic AI, RAG)

Prerequisite: You should have a basic understanding of deep learning before reading this paper. I’ve created the “Before LLMs” series, which brings together some of the best free resources for learning deep learning fundamentals.

I highly recommend going through these materials before starting the paper. At a minimum, complete the first 4 weeks of the series so you have the foundational knowledge needed to understand the concepts in the paper.

Week1(Computer Vision)

    AlexNet: https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2012/file/c399862d3b9d6b76c8436e924a68c45b-Paper.pdf?utm_source=Securitylab.ru
    VGGNet: https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.1556
    ResNet: https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03385

                                                                    Week2(NLP)

                                                       

    Word2Vec: https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.3781
    Seq2Seq:https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.3215
    Attention: https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.0473

                                                                  Week3(NLP)

    Attention is all you need:  https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.03762
    BERT: https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04805
    GPT 1: https://cdn.openai.com/research-covers/language-unsupervised/language_understanding_paper.pdf

                                                              Week4(CV)

     ViT: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.11929
    Swin Transformer: https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.14030
    PVT: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.12122

